# Personal-identifier deny list for scripts/scan_public_safety.py.
#
# D-2 of docs/DIRECTION.md: zero personal data in the codebase. This file is
# loaded by the scanner by default (tree, artifact and history modes) and is
# unioned with XPST_PUBLIC_SAFETY_DENYLIST, so the gate enforces it in CI with
# no environment plumbing.
#
# Format: one banned token per line, matched case-insensitively on word
# boundaries in the publishable tree and in built artifacts, and reported
# (never gating) in git history. '#' starts a comment; blank lines are
# ignored. Findings never echo the matched value.
#
# This file is the list of banned names, not personal data: it is the one
# tracked file the scan exempts from its own deny list.

